docs/debate/fable_r3.md:1:# Fable, Round 3: Drape, delivered seller-side and by extension
docs/debate/fable_r3.md:3:One finding reframes everything: cloth-v4 kept colour but changed silhouette (ruffle vs cape) on hand-recoloured references. The Round 2 "recolour locally, render three colourways" step is dead. The only party with real, clean colourway shots is the seller. That is the argument for the pivot.
docs/debate/fable_r3.md:7:**Strengthens the entry.** Reliability scores as Design (complete product); seller pre-flight scores as Tech depth (VTO as automated asset QA, which nobody else will show). **Strengthens the business.** This is how VTO is actually sold: catalogue integration, retailer pays, shopper never pays.
docs/debate/fable_r3.md:9:**What the seller does** (one form page, not a CMS): upload one clean, front-facing, single-garment shot per colourway; pick category (upper/lower/full/outer); confirm the dominant colour we extract locally; we map it to palette families (suits warm/cool) automatically, seller may override; press "pre-flight".
docs/debate/fable_r3.md:11:**Seller-time YouCam calls:** optional pre-flight Clothes VTO per colourway on a neutral model photo (synthetic or owner-consented, never stock), 2u. It proves the asset renders with a stable shape and becomes the judge-mode cached asset app-flow already plans. **Buyer-time:** colour reading, their own try-on, makeup, jewelry, unchanged. Seller prep makes the buyer render reliable and the catalogue free; it does not remove the buyer's 2u own-body try-on.
docs/debate/fable_r3.md:29:- **Seller Console** (Flutter web, `/seller`): colourway shots, category, local colour → palette family, pre-flight (2u/colourway), publish → "Drape-ready" badge and product ID.
docs/debate/fable_r3.md:31:- **Buyer Extension** (Chrome MV3, ~200 lines, no UI of its own): one click opens the hosted web app in a side panel with query params. Fast path: product is Drape-ready → clean asset, instant. Wild path: DOM extraction → backend checks → VTO.
docs/debate/fable_r3.md:34:**Calls and units.** Seller: pre-flight 2u/colourway. Buyer, once: Fitzpatrick 2u (demo) or Facial Color Tones 20u (premium), cached forever. Per look: Clothes VTO 2u; Makeup VTO 1u **on the selfie**, shown as a face close-up beside the outfit (designs around the untested ≥100 px face risk instead of testing it); Earrings or Necklace in the palette metal 1u. Session: 6–7u demo, 24–25u premium; wild path costs nothing extra.
docs/debate/fable_r3.md:36:**3-minute demo:** 0:00–0:20 seller uploads three colourway shots, pre-flight, badge. 0:20–1:10 buyer: selfie, undertone, drape reveal (incl. hijab drape), store re-sorted by face. 1:10–2:10 extension on a second synthetic store with no prep: click, image extracted, try-on, "match my face", gold earrings; then on the Drape-ready product, instant. 2:10–2:40 bundle to cart, Arabic RTL. 2:40–3:00 architecture card, roadmap.
docs/debate/fable_r3.md:42:**Build:** Day 1 backend proxy, cache, budget guard, buyer app steps 1–10 in demo mode with premium toggle. Day 2 seller console as one page with pre-flight; extension with the extraction ladder and the image-picker fallback. Day 3 two synthetic stores, judge persona cached, video.
docs/debate/fable_r3.md:44:**Roadmap only:** Amazon-specific adapters, Web Store listing, lower-body, batch catalogue import, Shopify app, makeup on the full-body output, seller analytics.
docs/debate/fable_r3.md:48:**Risk:** the wild path. Clothes VTO on arbitrary store imagery, and shape stability on real colourway pairs, are both untested; the one tested path varied silhouette.
docs/debate/fable_r3.md:50:**Test (not run; needs the owner's approval): 9 units.** Same buyer photo, four Clothes VTO calls: one clean flat-lay, one on-model single-person shot, one real colourway pair of the same SKU (8u); plus Makeup VTO on the selfie to confirm the face-path fallback (1u). Pass: the pair keeps silhouette, the on-model and flat-lay sources render. Fail on the pair: drop colourway comparison for good, verdict stays in the drape overlay. Fail on on-model: wild path ships behind the image picker only.
