docs/debate/fable_r1.md:18:- **Mechanism:** in-person seasonal colour analysis (a $150–300 service, huge on TikTok) is literally holding fabric drapes against the face. Facial Color Tones gives undertone; a deterministic palette table maps it to garment colourways and foundation/lip shades. The catalogue is *filtered and re-rendered* by a measurement of your face: fashion colourway and beauty shade come from one API output. Not "AI picks for you"; a rule table a colourist would sign. Hijab bonus: draping fabric around the face is exactly what a hijab does, so hijab colour choice works as a recoloured drape overlay with no hijab API.
docs/debate/fable_r1.md:19:- **API chain / units:** Facial Color Tones (20) → locally hue-shift the garment image into the winning and losing colourways (free) → Clothes VTO x4 (8) → Makeup VTO lip + foundation (1–2). About 30 units per session, cached per user; around 30 judge sessions from the pool after testing.
docs/debate/fable_r1.md:21:- **Riskiest assumption:** Clothes VTO renders a hue-shifted garment faithfully, and the undertone output is granular enough to map. De-risk in order: 4 Clothes VTO calls on recoloured garments (8) + 1 Fitzpatrick as proxy (2) + 1 Makeup (1) = 11 units; only then spend the single 20-unit Color Tones call.
docs/debate/fable_r1.md:27:- **Mechanism:** every VTO assumes the shopper is the wearer. Gifting breaks that. The giver chooses; the recipient tries on and edits before dispatch ("approve before ship"). Beauty + fashion are one object: a gift set rendered on one face.
docs/debate/fable_r1.md:28:- **API chain / units:** Earrings (1) + Necklace (1) + Ring (1) + Scarf or Bag (2) + Makeup lip (1) = about 6 per session; around 150 sessions. Persist the result image at completion, since results vanish after 24 h and the link is opened later.
docs/debate/fable_r1.md:30:- **Riskiest assumption:** jewelry VTO looks good on ordinary selfies, including hijabi faces where earrings may be hidden. De-risk: 5 Earrings + 5 Necklace calls = 10 units.
docs/debate/fable_r1.md:36:- **Mechanism:** the cart is a calendar. Skin Analysis concerns set what to buy *now*; Clothes, Hairstyle and Makeup VTO set the look for the day. Fashion and beauty are sequenced by a deadline. Egyptian weddings are three events (henna, katb el-ketab, wedding): three looks.
docs/debate/fable_r1.md:37:- **API chain / units:** Skin Analysis (~16) + Clothes VTO (2) + Hairstyle (2) + Makeup (1–2) = about 22; around 40 sessions.
docs/debate/fable_r1.md:38:- **Commerce:** the wedding is Egypt's largest consumer spend event; bridal boutiques and pharmacies want the pre-purchase schedule.
docs/debate/fable_r1.md:46:Switch trigger: if the 11-unit de-risk shows Clothes VTO smearing recoloured garments, fall to B: 6 units a session, no unproven rendering.
docs/debate/fable_r5.md:5:Drape's only dead end is the honest one: "None of this store's colours match yet." When no colourway of a garment is "Yours", the buyer taps **See it in Terracotta (your colour)**. Drape recolours the seller's own clean shot with **YouCam AI Fabric** (task name and params to confirm in the docs on day 1; the swatch is a flat PNG of the palette hex), renders that unsold colourway on her body with Clothes VTO beside the colour she would have settled for, labels it "not sold yet", and offers **Ask Noor Modest to make it in Terracotta**. The store gets a `drape:colour-request` event and a console table, *Terracotta: 14 requests, 11 warm-palette buyers*, with **Add as colourway (draft)**, which uses the Fabric render as the draft shot. The catalogue stops being the ceiling of the try-on.
docs/debate/fable_r5.md:9:- **Technical:** one reading drives a four-API chain (Color Tones → Fabric → Clothes VTO → Makeup), and Fabric attacks the gate-1 failure (hand recolours drifted in shape). A store-level render cache makes VTO an asset pipeline.
docs/debate/fable_r5.md:10:- **Design:** the empty state becomes the strongest screen; the buyer → store → catalogue loop closes inside the product.
docs/debate/fable_r5.md:18:## 4. YouCam APIs and units
docs/debate/fable_r5.md:22:| Fabric recolour of the seller's shot | store, cached per product × shot hash × hex | 2, once |
docs/debate/fable_r5.md:23:| Clothes VTO of the recolour on the buyer | buyer | 2 |
docs/debate/fable_r5.md:24:| Day-1 gate (2 Fabric + 1 VTO) | development, owner-approved | ≈ 6 |
docs/debate/fable_r5.md:27:Per buyer 2u (4u for the first to ask that colour on that product); per store 2u per requested colour; live: one request per session. Build spend ≈ 16u of the ~550 outside the reserve. Replay: the warm persona opens the new product, no colourway reads Yours, `persona/request_<product>_terracotta.jpg` serves the beat, 0u.
docs/debate/fable_r5.md:31:- **Day 1:** confirm Fabric params; run the gate (≈ 6u, approval first); add `fabric` to `YouCamTask` in `backend/src/youcam.ts`.
docs/debate/fable_r5.md:32:- **Day 2:** `backend/src/state.ts`: job type `recolor` with a store-level cache key, `POST /v1/sessions/me/requests` (reserve 4u, 2u on cache hit), `GET /v1/admin/requests` grouped by product × colour × undertone; `embed/v1.js` emits `drape:colour-request`; third product and fixtures.
docs/debate/fable_r5.md:33:- **Day 3:** Flutter: `shop_screen.dart` chip; `compare_screen.dart` "not sold yet" variant; `look_screen.dart` ask button; `seller_screen.dart` requests table and draft colourway.
docs/debate/fable_r5.md:34:- **Day 4:** tests (reserve amounts, cache hit, RTL), EN/AR copy, README and Devpost rows, video beat.
docs/debate/fable_r5.md:35:- **Cut order:** draft-colourway button first (counts stay), then the live request path (replay only, labelled).
docs/debate/fable_r5.md:43:Fabric may be pattern-only, add texture to a solid abaya, or miss the hex; the recolour may still drift in VTO. Day-1 verdict: pass if the garment's median colour is within ΔE 15 of the requested hex and the silhouette overlaps the source at IoU ≥ 0.95. Fallback A: Background Removal (1u) for the mask, LAB recolour locally, then VTO. Fallback B: the request at 0u as a swatch on the drape overlay. The seller loop survives both.
